  "id": "apraxia-of-speech",
  "term": "apraxia of speech",
  "definition": "Apraxia of speech, especially childhood apraxia of speech, is a motor speech disorder in which a person has trouble planning or programming the movements needed for speech. It can show up as inconsistent speech errors, difficulty moving smoothly between sounds or syllables, and problems with stress patterns in words.",
